    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0565" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11663a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I send despatch just received from the Secretary of the Navy: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Mayo reports, April 9, 5 p.m.:</p>
                        <p>“This forenoon Mexican soldiers arrested paymaster and whaleboat’s crew
                            of <hi rendition="#italic">Dolphin</hi>, part of whom were in boat with
                            flag flying, marched them two blocks through streets, then back to boat,
                            and there released them. General Zaragoza expressed regret verbally.</p>
                        <p>“In view of publicity of event, I have called for formal disavowal and
                            apology, punishment of officer in charge Mexican squad, and salute to
                            American flag within 24 hours from 6 p.m., Thursday.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">“Mayo.”</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I do not see that Mayo could have done otherwise. I await instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
